<!--
  Dimensions: read and type the body's overall size on its own X, Y and Z.

  A technical-drawing DIMENSION, not a tool: two extension lines, a measure line
  between them and a tick at each end — the draughting convention every engineer
  already reads, and deliberately not an arrow, a cube or a ruler. The body it
  measures is the light rectangle behind it, so the glyph says "the size of that
  thing" rather than "a length".

  Drawn white and tinted at use; see EditorControlStyles.iconButton().
-->
